{
 "lang": "en",
 "duration": 79.90125,
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 4.38,
   "text": "The explosion of depression and anxiety in our society today is because people actually"
  },
  {
   "start": 4.38,
   "end": 7.7,
   "text": "don't know the meaning of their lives, much less so in previous generations."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.8,
   "end": 9.0,
   "text": "Tons of data show this."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.2,
   "end": 10.68,
   "text": "And furthermore, we're not even looking."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.94,
   "end": 11.5,
   "text": "Why not?"
  },
  {
   "start": 11.62,
   "end": 12.36,
   "text": "I'll tell you why not."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.44,
   "end": 14.64,
   "text": "We figured out a way to eliminate boredom."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.76,
   "end": 15.16,
   "text": "How?"
  },
  {
   "start": 15.28,
   "end": 19.0,
   "text": "The answer is that thing in your pocket with the screen, which you take out even"
  },
  {
   "start": 19.0,
   "end": 22.26,
   "text": "when you're standing on the street corner waiting for the light to change, is like,"
  },
  {
   "start": 22.34,
   "end": 24.36,
   "text": "I might have to wait here for 15 seconds."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.94,
   "end": 28.7,
   "text": "If every time you're slightly bored, you pull out your phone, it's going to get"
  },
  {
   "start": 28.7,
   "end": 33.44,
   "text": "harder and harder for you to find meaning, and that's the recipe for depression and"
  },
  {
   "start": 33.44,
   "end": 38.4,
   "text": "anxiety and a sense of hollowness, which, by the way, are all through the roof."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.56,
   "end": 38.98,
   "text": "I get it."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.98,
   "end": 39.66,
   "text": "You don't want to be bored."
  },
  {
   "start": 39.76,
   "end": 40.48,
   "text": "You need to be bored."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.72,
   "end": 41.38,
   "text": "Be bored more."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.58,
   "end": 44.02,
   "text": "Tomorrow, when you go to the gym in the morning after you wake up, don't take"
  },
  {
   "start": 44.02,
   "end": 44.44,
   "text": "your phone."
  },
  {
   "start": 44.52,
   "end": 45.3,
   "text": "Can you handle it?"
  },
  {
   "start": 45.3,
   "end": 46.32,
   "text": "Just being in your head?"
  },
  {
   "start": 46.48,
   "end": 48.76,
   "text": "I promise you, you'll have your most interesting ideas."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.04,
   "end": 51.24,
   "text": "Commute with nothing, not even the radio."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.36,
   "end": 52.08,
   "text": "Can you do that?"
  },
  {
   "start": 52.24,
   "end": 56.92,
   "text": "Start getting better at periods that are 15 minutes and longer of boredom."
  },
  {
   "start": 56.92,
   "end": 58.8,
   "text": "And watch your life change."
  },
  {
   "start": 59.12,
   "end": 62.14,
   "text": "Number one, you'll be less bored with ordinary things in your life."
  },
  {
   "start": 62.26,
   "end": 65.22,
   "text": "If you get better at the skill of boredom, you'll be less bored with your job."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.4,
   "end": 66.84,
   "text": "You'll be less bored with your relationships."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.02,
   "end": 69.38,
   "text": "You'll be less bored with the things that are going on around you."
  },
  {
   "start": 69.48,
   "end": 73.26,
   "text": "But more importantly, you'll start digging into the biggest questions in your life."
  },
  {
   "start": 73.72,
   "end": 79.2,
   "text": "Purpose, meaning, coherence, significance, and who knows, you might just get happier."
  }
 ],
